1. Ground Warfare – Combat conducted primarily by land forces.
2. Infantry Warfare – Combat involving soldiers fighting primarily as ground troops.
3. Armored Warfare – Combat involving tanks and other armored fighting vehicles.
4. Mechanized Warfare – Ground operations using armored and motorized vehicles.
5. Mountain Warfare – Military operations in mountainous terrain.
6. Urban Warfare – Combat in cities, towns, and densely populated areas.
7. Jungle Warfare – Military operations in dense tropical environments.
8. Desert Warfare – Combat in arid and desert environments.
9. Arctic Warfare – Military operations in extremely cold and icy environments.
10. Trench Warfare – Combat involving fortified defensive positions and trench systems.
11. Guerrilla Warfare – Irregular warfare involving smaller forces fighting larger conventional forces.
12. Amphibious Warfare – Military operations involving movement between sea and land.

