1. Air-to-Air Warfare – Combat between aircraft.
2. Air-to-Ground Warfare – Aircraft conducting operations against targets on land.
3. Strategic Bombing – Air operations intended to affect an opponent's strategic capabilities.
4. Close Air Support (CAS) – Air support coordinated with friendly ground forces.
5. Air Superiority Warfare – Efforts to establish control of the airspace.
6. Air Interdiction – Air operations intended to disrupt enemy forces and resources before they reach the battlefield.
7. Electronic Warfare (EW) – Military use of the electromagnetic spectrum to protect friendly systems and disrupt opposing systems.
8. Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses (SEAD) – Operations intended to reduce threats from enemy air-defense systems.
9. Counter-Air Operations – Operations intended to reduce or neutralize an opposing air force.
10. Aerial Reconnaissance – Gathering information using aircraft and airborne sensors.
11. Drone Warfare – Military operations involving remotely piloted or autonomous aircraft.
12. Airborne Warfare – Military operations involving troops delivered by aircraft, including parachute operations.

