1. Naval Warfare – Combat conducted by naval forces at sea.
2. Surface Warfare – Combat involving ships operating on the ocean's surface.
3. Submarine Warfare – Military operations involving submarines.
4. Anti-Submarine Warfare (ASW) – Detecting, tracking, and countering submarines.
5. Amphibious Warfare – Operations involving naval forces moving troops and equipment onto land.
6. Mine Warfare – Naval operations involving sea mines and mine countermeasures.
7. Maritime Interdiction – Operations intended to stop or inspect maritime traffic.
8. Carrier Warfare – Naval aviation operations conducted from aircraft carriers.
9. Coastal Warfare – Military operations conducted near coastlines.
10. Blockade Warfare – Restricting access to ports or maritime routes.

# 5. Modern and technological warfare

